In addition to banning images of self-harm, Instagram said it will not promote non-[g]raphic self-harm-related content like healed scars or through hashtags or the explore tab, though they’re not removing the content entirely as not to “stigmatise or isolate people who may be in distress and posting self-harm-related content as a cry for help”.
Mr Russell was buoyed by Instagram’s commitment, and in an interview with the BBC called on other social media to follow suit.

